WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.846
A drone program may manage still imagery, video, thermal files, telemetry, flight logs, maps, models, inspection notes, annotations, and reports.

00:00:10.846 --> 00:00:19.673
Every product should remain linked to the mission, aircraft, sensor, time, location confidence, and responsible reviewer.

00:00:19.673 --> 00:00:25.979
Use consistent file names, mission identifiers, folder structures, and metadata rules.

00:00:25.979 --> 00:00:29.762
Preserve originals separately from processed outputs.

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:36.572
Record transformations such as stitching, enhancement, redaction, annotation, conversion, or artificial-intelligence assistance.

00:00:36.572 --> 00:00:43.887
Storage design addresses capacity, performance, encryption, backup, recovery, retention, legal hold, and deletion.

00:00:43.887 --> 00:00:54.732
Exports and temporary working copies deserve the same protection as the central repository because they may contain equivalent sensitive data.

00:00:54.732 --> 00:01:02.047
G I S integration can connect observations to authorized maps and asset records.

00:01:02.047 --> 00:01:07.344
Position metadata should be validated when navigation anomalies occur.

00:01:07.344 --> 00:01:14.154
Dashboards should communicate coverage, status, findings, confidence, and gaps without overstating precision.

00:01:14.154 --> 00:01:20.964
Reporting workflows distinguish direct observation, automated output, analyst judgment, and specialist diagnosis.

00:01:20.964 --> 00:01:30.296
Quality review should check evidence references, privacy, accuracy, uncertainty, and whether the product answers the mission request.

00:01:30.296 --> 00:01:36.097
Protect sensitive imagery of people, property, facilities, infrastructure, and operations.

00:01:36.097 --> 00:01:46.438
Limit distribution to legitimate recipients, control public release, and retain only what policy, law, evidence, and operational need justify.

00:01:46.438 --> 00:01:56.779
Where evidence integrity matters, preserve collection and processing lineage: who captured, transferred, transformed, reviewed, approved, and exported each product.

00:01:56.779 --> 00:02:04.598
This supports correction and accountability without claiming that every operational image is forensic evidence.
